[THINKING]● Thinking: **Summarizing custom domain implementation and testing**

I'll organize a detailed summary highlighting the new custom domain workflow features with precise file references for backend APIs, job scheduling, certificate handling, UI views, infra, and documentation. I'll also cover the executed tests including linting and targeted Maven runs, explaining test failures due to unrelated suites in the large test runs, and outline logical next steps around verifying targeted tests and certificate secrets. This way, the user gets a clear, concise breakdown of the changes, validations, and ongoing considerations.
[RUNNING]● Message: **Custom Domain Workflow**
- Added tenant-scoped REST resource that issues verification tokens, surfaces DNS instructions, and enforces ownership for list/get/create/delete operations so admins can manage domains directly (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/CustomDomainResource.java:41-214`). The accompanying Flyway migration persists status/error/certificate metadata for each domain (`modules/core-platform/src/main/resources/db/migrations/V20260132__custom_domain_ssl_automation.sql:18-70`), and the JPA model reflects those new columns for downstream services (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/data/models/CustomDomain.java:33-94`).
- DomainValidationJob now drives the automation loop: it seeds tenant context, enforces an exponential retry schedule, marks failures with actionable messages, and fires `CustomDomainVerified` when DNS proves ownership; failures move domains into the `FAILED` state so the UI/runbook can warn operators (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/jobs/DomainValidationJob.java:29-299`). CertificateEventHandler emits the cert-manager manifest while infra adds prod/staging ClusterIssuers plus RBAC so cert-manager can satisfy those requests (`modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/jobs/CertificateEventHandler.java:21-177`, `infra/kustomize/base/cert-manager/issuer.yaml:1-150`).
- Platform Admin UI now exposes a Domain Settings view that lists each domain, shows DNS instructions for `PENDING`, displays actionable error text for `FAILED`, and warns about expiring certificates (`modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/modules/platform/views/DomainSettingsView.vue:1-400`).
- Operations runbook documents the full workflow—including state meanings, DNS troubleshooting, job triggers, and cert-manager commands—so on-call staff can remediate failures without diving into code (`docs/operations/runbook.md:1265-1384`).
- API and job coverage was added: the REST test suite now drives requests through the tenant access gateway (cache invalidation + Host headers) and asserts all CRUD/status cases (`modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/CustomDomainResourceTest.java:1-215`), while the job tests exercise retry counting, state transitions, and timestamp updates (`modules/core-platform/src/test/java/villagecompute/storefront/jobs/DomainValidationJobTest.java:97-180`). Task tracker updated per protocol (`.codemachine/artifacts/tasks/tasks_I5.json:1-228`).

**Testing**
- `node tools/lint.cjs`
- `./mvnw -pl modules/core-platform -Dtest=CustomDomainResourceTest,DomainValidationJobTest test`
- `node tools/test.cjs` *(fails because the pre-existing suite still contains 100+ unrelated regressions such as StripeIntegrationTest, CatalogJobServiceTest, StoreCreditServiceTest, etc.; see the command output for the full list)*

